IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- TIME, for the Cat Act 2011 (WA).
--
-- The Cat Act counts days ("within 7 days after"), working days ("within 3
-- working days of the cat entering"), months ("within the period of 12
-- months before") and years ("within the previous 3 years", "6 months of
-- age", "under 18 years of age"). It defines none of them. The rules below
-- come from the Interpretation Act 1984 ss 5, 61 and 62
-- (inputs/interpretation-act-1984-extract.txt), which apply to every
-- written law, and one is an encoding choice recorded as fork F-01.
--
-- Public holidays are an INPUT: a list of dates. No library ships the WA
-- calendar (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972), and "a public holiday
-- throughout the State or in that part of the State which is relevant"
-- (s 61(2)) depends on where the event happened.

§ `Time`

§§ `The period this encoding states the law for`

-- inputs/PROVENANCE.md: the Act consolidation 00-l0-01 is current from
-- 25 September 2025 and the Regulations consolidation 02-b0-00 from
-- 24 July 2025. Earlier versions were not fetched, so for an earlier date
-- this encoding has no source. That is the encoder's answer, not the law's,
-- and so it is a refusal (phrasebook 11.5), never the current text answering
-- for a past date.
@ref inputs/PROVENANCE.md, "In-force statements"
GIVETH A DATE
`the first date this encoding states the law for` MEANS YMD 2025 9 25

@ref inputs/PROVENANCE.md, "In-force statements"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025` MEANS
    REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025: this encoding states the Cat Act 2011 as consolidated from 25 September 2025 and the Cat Regulations 2012 as consolidated from 24 July 2025"

-- Every decision that is about a day reads it through this gate.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law is encoded for` d MEANS
    IF d AT LEAST `the first date this encoding states the law for`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025`

§§ `Interpretation Act 1984 s 61 — days`

-- s 61(2): "excluded day means Saturday, Sunday, public service holiday,
-- and a bank holiday or public holiday throughout the State or in that part
-- of the State which is relevant ..." Public service, bank and public
-- holidays all arrive in the one input list.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(2)
GIVEN d        IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an excluded day` d `given` holidays IF
        `is weekend` d
    OR  elem d holidays

-- s 61(1)(e): "where the time limited for the doing of a thing expires or
-- falls upon an excluded day, the thing may be done on the next day that is
-- not an excluded day".
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(e)
GIVEN d        IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day from` d `that is not excluded, given` holidays MEANS
    IF   `an excluded day` d `given` holidays
    THEN `the first day from` (d PLUS 1) `that is not excluded, given` holidays
    ELSE d

-- s 61(1)(b): "where a period of time is expressed to be reckoned from, or
-- after, a specified day, that day shall not be included in the period";
-- then s 61(1)(e). So "within 7 days after X" closes at the end of X + 7,
-- moved forward past any excluded day.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN n        IS A NUMBER
      d        IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to act within` n `days after` d `given` holidays MEANS
    `the first day from` (d PLUS n) `that is not excluded, given` holidays

§§ `Working days — fork F-01`

-- "working day" is used in Cat Act ss 32(b) and 34(1)(a), (b)(i) and is
-- defined nowhere that reaches the Cat Act. The Local Government Act 1995
-- defines it only "In this Schedule" (Sch 4.1A cl 1,
-- inputs/local-government-act-1995-extract.txt), so Cat Act s 3(2) does not
-- carry it across. FORK F-01: this encoding takes the ordinary meaning, a
-- day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday in the input list —
-- which happens to be the same set of days as s 61(2)'s excluded days, and
-- the same as the LG Act Sch 4.1A wording.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 32(b), s 34(1); fork F-01 in NOTES.md
GIVEN d        IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a working day` d `given` holidays IF
    NOT `an excluded day` d `given` holidays

-- The n-th working day after d, d itself not counted (s 61(1)(b)).
GIVEN n        IS A NUMBER
      d        IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `working days after` d `given` holidays MEANS
    IF   n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE `the date` (n MINUS `one if a working day`) `working days after` (d PLUS 1) `given` holidays
    WHERE
        `one if a working day` MEANS IF `a working day` (d PLUS 1) `given` holidays THEN 1 ELSE 0

§§ `Interpretation Act 1984 s 62 — months and years`

-- s 62(3): a period of n months "shall be reckoned from the date on which
-- it is to begin to the date numerically corresponding, less one, in the
-- ... successive month thereafter or, if there is no such corresponding
-- date, to the last day of the latter month." s 5: "year means a period of
-- 12 months".
--
-- What the Act needs is the FIRST DAY AFTER such a period: the day a cat
-- "has reached 6 months of age", the day a person is no longer "under 18
-- years of age". That is the numerically corresponding date where there is
-- one, and otherwise the first day of the next month (a cat born on
-- 31 August reaches 6 months on 1 March, because the 6 months ran to the
-- last day of February). `add months` would answer 28 February — a day early.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 62(2), (3); s 5 "year"
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day after a period of` n `months beginning on` d MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY d AT MOST `Days in month` (DATE_MONTH `first of the latter month`) (DATE_YEAR `first of the latter month`)
    THEN Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH `first of the latter month`) (DATE_YEAR `first of the latter month`)
    ELSE Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `first of the latter month` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `first of the latter month`)
    WHERE
        -- Date rolls a month past 12 into the next year, which is wanted here.
        `first of the latter month` MEANS Date 1 (DATE_MONTH d PLUS n) (DATE_YEAR d)

-- A being born on b has reached n months of age on d.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      b IS A DATE
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reached` n `months of age, if born on` b `, on` d IF
    d AT LEAST `the day after a period of` n `months beginning on` b

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      b IS A DATE
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `under` n `years of age, if born on` b `, on` d IF
    NOT `reached` (n TIMES 12) `months of age, if born on` b `, on` d

-- "within the previous 3 years", "within the period of 12 months before":
-- an event on e falls within the n months before d when it is on or before d
-- and after the date n months before d. FORK F-02 records the one-day edge:
-- an event on the very anniversary is outside.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
      e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the` n `months before` d `, an event on` e IF
        e AT MOST d
    AND d LESS THAN `the day after a period of` n `months beginning on` e

§§ `A thing to be done within n days after an event`

-- Used by every "within 7 days after ..." duty in the Act (ss 13, 15, 20,
-- 24, 25, 40). On day d, the duty has been contravened when the thing was
-- not done by the last day for doing it (s 61(1)(b), (e)) — either it was
-- done later, or it has not been done and that last day has passed.
GIVEN n        IS A NUMBER
      e        IS A DATE
      done     IS A MAYBE DATE
      d        IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not done within` n `days after` e `, done on` done `, as at` d `given` holidays IF
    CONSIDER done
    WHEN JUST m  THEN IF   m AT MOST d
                      THEN m GREATER THAN `the last day`
                      ELSE d GREATER THAN `the last day`     -- done, but only after d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN d GREATER THAN `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day to act within` n `days after` e `given` holidays
